---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Building Scalable APIs with Node.js | Blog">
  <main class="section">
    <article class="container post-content">
      <p><a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to Blog</a></p>
      <h1>Building Scalable APIs with Node.js</h1>
      <p class="meta">Mar 12, 2026</p>
      <p>Scalable APIs start with clear boundaries and predictable behavior.</p>
      <p>
        A maintainable approach keeps controllers thin, moves business logic to services, and includes
        robust input validation from day one.
      </p>
      <p>
        By investing in observability and consistent error responses, teams can scale their platform
        without slowing down feature delivery.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post-content {
    max-width: 760px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); margin-top: -0.25rem; }
  .back-link { color: var(--secondary); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
